From 8d4b2c9f0a3e2f1b5d6c7b8a9b0c1d2e3f4a5b6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Balaharish Saravanan <balaharish0202@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:15:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(core): implement fine-grained MCP tool approval policies and timeout hooks

When an agent requests approval for tool execution (e.g., file writes or
terminal commands), sessions currently suspend indefinitely if the user
does not interact with the approval prompt.

This commit adds:
- Configurable ToolApprovalPolicy schema (autoApprove, timeoutMs, defaultAction)
- Automatic approval for read-only tools (read_file, search_files)
- Non-blocking timeout rejection hooks that prevent session hangs and return
  a descriptive rejection event back into the turn loop.

Signed-off-by: Balaharish Saravanan <balaharish0202@gmail.com>
